=== EVENT_SHAPE ===
Phase-42 SSE typed envelope (per-signal change):

  event: signal_change
  data: {
    "vehicle_id": <int64>,
    "field":      <proto field name, e.g. "VehicleSpeed">,
    "kind":       <protomodel.ValueKind discriminator (int)>,
    "value":      <typed primitive: bool/number/string/time.Time/enum>,
    "ts":         <RFC3339 timestamp from signal.Value.Timestamp>
  }

The SignalChangeEvent struct is marshalled directly by EventHub.Broadcast
which prepends "event: signal_change\ndata: ...\n\n". The "value" field
carries signal.Value.Raw verbatim — json.Marshal handles every concrete
type the codec emits without reflection.

Cross-pod fanout: when redisCache is wired via SubscribeRedis, the same
typed envelope flows through Redis Pub/Sub channel "vehicle_signals"
(preserved per ARCHITECTURE.md ADR for the layered live-state contract).
SubscribeRedis is unchanged from prompt 0064 — it transparently forwards
any payload format published by PublishSignals.

The legacy aggregated "vehicle_update" Broadcast emitted by
TelemetryHandler.broadcastSSE in telemetry_handler_ingest.go remains the
batch-update path for whole-vehicle map snapshots. SignalChangeEvent /
BroadcastSignalChange is the per-field complement — added now so future
prompts in the consumer-migration series can wire signal.Store change
notifications into the SSE channel without re-touching sse_handler.go.

=== UNIT_TEST ===
Test scope rationale (deferred test variance):

  The prompt's allowed-files list is exactly:
    - internal/api/sse_handler.go
    - this log

  This excludes internal/api/api_test.go (where the existing EventHub
  TestEventHub_SubscribeAndBroadcast / _Unsubscribe / _MultipleClients
  tests live) and forbids creating a sibling internal/api/sse_handler_test.go
  (the gate's path-substring regex would reject it).

  The existing EventHub tests in api_test.go continue to pass because
  this prompt is purely additive: NewEventHub, Subscribe, Broadcast,
  ClientCount, SubscribeRedis, and SSEHandler retain their exact prior
  signatures and behaviour. Only two new exported names are introduced:
    - type SignalChangeEvent struct
    - (*EventHub).BroadcastSignalChange

  go test -race ./internal/api/... is run below as the gate test, which
  exercises:
    - EventHub subscribe/broadcast/unsubscribe paths (api_test.go:372+)
    - typed envelope contract via the Go type checker (compile must
      succeed; mismatched signal.Value or ValueKind references would
      fail the build before tests even run)
    - downstream callers of EventHub.Broadcast (alert_handler_rules,
      automation_events, lifetime_handler, telemetry_handler_ingest,
      router) which all keep their existing call sites untouched.

  An end-to-end test that wires BroadcastSignalChange through to a real
  HTTP SSE flusher belongs in a follow-on prompt that may modify
  api_test.go (e.g. a "consumer-api-sse-integration" prompt). Adding it
  here would violate the allowed-files contract.

